                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "mees"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dfb9a58b-2180-3be4-aea8-32b5c134ac8f",
                        "entry_id": "5cd8c6a4-b65a-398b-9aa6-a556f96f5d79",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Chinese-style wheat noodles."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Malaysia",
                            "Singapore",
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ab6bcb90-ab39-412c-9187-53bb56e732a1",
                                "sense_id": "dfb9a58b-2180-3be4-aea8-32b5c134ac8f",
                                "text": "He watched with pleasure the food-sellers swirling the frying mee round in their kualis over primitive charcoal fires."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f59996e6-2c45-309a-b496-5b0b79ea0d78",
                        "entry_id": "5cd8c6a4-b65a-398b-9aa6-a556f96f5d79",
                        "glosses": [
                            "With a descriptive word: a dish containing Chinese-style wheat noodles."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Malaysia",
                            "Singapore",
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0aa61a2f-bb98-4749-9d50-acb3e75feff7",
                                "sense_id": "f59996e6-2c45-309a-b496-5b0b79ea0d78",
                                "text": "curry mee    prawn mee soup"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c044d35e-3685-49b4-9229-8c125da48bd4",
                                "sense_id": "f59996e6-2c45-309a-b496-5b0b79ea0d78",
                                "text": "We were confronted by a large dish piled with a startling mixture of spaghetti, bamboo shoots, sliced prawns, and tiny cubes of pork […] Its name […] was mee. Mee is a favourite dish of the Chinese, and is on sale at all hours of the day and night."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d760a975-b4f4-415f-a817-8e1fa56bfb6a",
                                "sense_id": "f59996e6-2c45-309a-b496-5b0b79ea0d78",
                                "text": "Hokkien Prawn Mee – Pork and prawns in yellow noodles. […] Mushroom Mee – Noodles with Chinese mushrooms, minced pork and green vegetables."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "88b3edb3-0015-45c9-b3e8-1d919a9a570d",
                                "sense_id": "f59996e6-2c45-309a-b496-5b0b79ea0d78",
                                "text": "Penang-style prawn mee is spicier and is usually served with more pork than Singapore-style prawn mee. Like Singapore-style prawn mee, the Hokkien mee in this recipe can be combined with fine rice vermicelli."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "459a34df-0b34-4901-9559-87ebdf14b9ef",
                                "sense_id": "f59996e6-2c45-309a-b496-5b0b79ea0d78",
                                "text": "Braised. Thick. Heavy. These are the key words people associate with lor mee, and it's all true! And it's so dam shiok! If you're a fan of braised dishes with that dark gooey sauce, you'll love this lor mee recipe."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8efc72e1-111a-469e-863f-5251ad39763b",
                                "sense_id": "f59996e6-2c45-309a-b496-5b0b79ea0d78",
                                "text": "My former student's kouyteav sachko (mee Champa) is not just any other mee soup. In it is one person's constant reminder of his/her identity heightened in its unique ingredients, taste and flavour and presented vis-a-vis other types of mee soup available in restaurants, kopitiams, hawkers' stalls or at home."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
